        "description": "## Repro\n\nRun `pnpm deploy:dev:topology` with a prepared development topology. After the in-south app Worker deploys, Wrangler rejects the in-south MCP Worker upload with Cloudflare validation error 10021: `Uncaught TypeError: Class2 is not a constructor`. The stack starts in `zod@4.4.3/v4/core/api.js` `_custom`, called from `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.29.0` `src/types.ts:22`.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe MCP Worker deploys with the rest of the topology and preserves the existing MCP authentication behavior.\n\n## Actual\n\nThe full topology deploy stops at `skillplane-mcp-dev-in-south`. SKI-16's app and DataFn canary required selective `--only app,datafn` deployment. `pnpm smoke:dev` still confirms the previously deployed MCP endpoint requires authentication.\n\n## Useful entry points\n\n`packages/mcp/wrangler.jsonc`, `scripts/lib/development-topology-deployment.mjs`, and the MCP SDK/Zod package versions. Reproduce in a Wrangler dry-run and a dev upload before changing production topology.",
