1\. Browser reads fail preflight <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code>

<pre>
<b><i>regional-datafn-worker</i></b> configures <b><i>withDatafnRegionalCors</i></b> to allow only
<b><i>x-skillplane-workspace-id</i></b>, omitting the <b><i>x-datafn-route-ticket</i></b> header required by its own
admission check. Because the DataFn client sends that header to a regional origin distinct from the
app origin, browsers preflight the request and reject the actual read when the header is absent from
the allowed-header response.
</pre>


<details>
<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>

```
## Issue description
Browser-originated regional DataFn reads send `x-datafn-route-ticket`, but the regional Worker CORS configuration does not allow that request header. The browser therefore blocks the cross-origin request during preflight before ticket verification can occur.

## Fix Focus Areas
- app/src/regional-datafn-worker.ts[75-78]

## Recommended Fix
Add `x-datafn-route-ticket` to the CORS allowed request headers passed to `withDatafnRegionalCors`. Also ensure every non-safelisted header sent by the regional client, including JSON `content-type` if the CORS helper does not allow it by default, is explicitly permitted; retain the existing single trusted app origin and do not enable credentials.
