P2: The connect-src host list duplicates the datafnEndpoint.httpUrl origins from deployment/topology.{production,development}.json, but nothing enforces that they stay in sync. Adding a new cell region to the topology (e.g. a future eu-west production cell) will silently disable direct reads for that region, because the browser fetch to the new origin is blocked by this CSP and the client falls back to the canonical gateway. This shared config also ships the dev hosts into the production app's CSP and the prod hosts into the dev app. Add a comment tying this list to the topology manifests (and update it whenever a region is added), or derive the origins from a single source of truth.

